DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     Function ddwwaarrff__aattttrr() retrieves the attribute descriptor for an attribute
     associated with the DWARF debugging information entry descriptor in argu‐
     ment _d_i_e.

     DWARF attribute descriptors are represented by value of the opaque type
     _D_w_a_r_f___A_t_t_r_i_b_u_t_e, see dwarf(3).

     Argument _a_t_t_r names the desired DWARF attribute.  Legal values for argu‐
     ment _a_t_t_r are those denoted by the DW_AT_* constants in the DWARF speci‐
     fication.

     Argument _a_t_p points to a location into which the returned attribute de‐
     scriptor will be written.  The returned descriptor may then be passed to
     the form query functions in the dwarf(3) API set to access the data asso‐
     ciated with the attribute.

     If argument _e_r_r is non-NULL, it will be used to return an error descrip‐
     tor in case of an error.

